    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0396" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20/831a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>)<anchor n="69"
                        xml:id="d260-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-03T19:00:00-05:00">April 3, 1935—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. I should appreciate receiving for my confidential information your personal
                    estimate of the political situation in Europe at the present time and of
                    probable developments as you foresee them.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d260-f1" n="69" type="source" xml:id="d260-f1-content">
                <p>The same telegram was sent, April 3, to the Ambassador in France (No. 117), and
                    in the United Kingdom (No. 77); on the following day a similar telegram was sent
                    to the Chargé in the Soviet Union (No. 74).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
